{
  "requirement": "Each requirement and example declaration badge has two adjacent links. Its\nkind (`req` or `example`) links to the declaration's anchor on the current\npage; its full name links to the evidence detail page. These segments stay\ntogether in one non-wrapping row, with no separate arrow link or plaintext evidence link.\nEach detail page links back to the declaration's anchored badge and to the\nindex. Reference badges continue to link to the declaration. These links\nresolve when a requirement name contains `.md`, as in\n`requirements.cli.mdbook`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.index.navigation`, and their assertions enforce each one.\n\n**Kind link and name link on each declaration badge**\n- `declaration_sections_contain_their_headers_and_markdown_bodies` checks the header of both a `req` and an `example` declaration. The kind link has `href=\"#habeas-{kind}-rules.{name}\"`, a title and an aria-label. The name link has `href=\"requirements-index/rules.{name}.html\"` and the title \"View evidence for ...\". The test also asserts that neither the header nor the hidden body contains `habeas-detail-icon`.\n- `mdbook_preprocessor_renders_definitions_between_stdin_and_stdout` runs the real binary. Each badge row has exactly two `</a>` elements, one `habeas-badge-kind` and one `habeas-badge-name`, with no `<svg`. It also checks the `#habeas-req-rules.ready` and `requirements-index/rules.ready.html` hrefs.\n- `declaration_badges_and_margin_controls_share_kind_colors`, `index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons` and `definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages` also check these links.\n\n**One non-wrapping row**\n- `declaration_badge_stylesheet_keeps_split_links_in_one_row` asserts the wrapper styles `inline-flex`, `flex-wrap: nowrap` and `white-space: nowrap`. It also asserts `flex-shrink: 0` on the links.\n- The stylesheet test and the single `habeas-definition-badge` span per declaration (counted in the repository test) cover the \"stay together in one row\" clause.\n\n**No separate arrow link or plaintext evidence link**\n- Tests assert `!contains(\"See evidence\")`, `!contains(\"<svg\")` and `!contains(\"habeas-detail-icon\")`.\n- The two-`</a>` count in the repository test also rules out an extra link.\n\n**Detail pages link back to the badge and to the index**\n- `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` asserts `[View definition](../../requirements/core.html#habeas-req-requirements.core.ready)`. It also asserts `[Requirements index](../requirements-index.html) · [View definition]`.\n- `definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages` checks the index link on every detail page. It checks the definition link for the `.md` name and for a nested chapter.\n- `index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons` checks the definition link for an example, `#habeas-example-more.cli%2Emdbook`.\n\n**Reference badges continue to link to the declaration**\n- `references_in_nested_chapters_link_to_the_requirement_definition` covers `impl`, `cite` and `test` badges from a nested chapter. It asserts `href=\"../requirements.html#habeas-req-requirements.ready\"`.\n- `citation_metadata_is_hidden_in_fenced_sections_and_preserved_in_details` covers the badge links in detail pages.\n\n**Names containing `.md`**\n- `links_preserve_requirement_names_containing_md` asserts the exact `%2Emd` escaping through `chapter_href` in both directions. That function builds the detail-page, definition and reference-badge links, so one check covers all three.\n- Several rendering tests use `cli.mdbook` and assert the escaped anchors and hrefs. These include the `id`/`href` pair, `requirements-index/rules.cli%2Emdbook.html` and `#habeas-req-rules.cli%2Emdbook`.\n\n**Escaping of the link target**\n- `definition_evidence_link_targets_are_escaped` is a related check on the evidence link's `href`.\n\nI found no obligation or named boundary case without a test. All the tests carry `{test}` references to `requirements.index.navigation`. I found no acknowledgments, and none are needed.",
  "references": "4e0e60c4f8a54bb02a235630bf39f7a53d1b2376299a4958a791682aff9a7597",
